//! The `text-decoration` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property sets the appearance of decorative lines on text. It is a shorthand for
//! `text-decoration-line`, `text-decoration-color`, `text-decoration-style`, and the newer
//! `text-decoration-thickness` property.
//!
//! Initial: text-decoration-color: currentcolor; text-decoration-style: solid; text-decoration-line:
//! none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: <'text-decoration-line'> || <'text-decoration-thickness'> || <'text-decoration-style'>
//! || <'text-decoration-color'>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#propdef-text-decoration
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-decoration
